# Tests

- Test observable behavior and public contracts, not private implementation.
- Use immutable builders with explicit overrides and no production data.
- Inject clocks, IDs, randomness, and I/O; never depend on test order.
- Prefer table-driven tests for variants and property tests for invariants.
- Use real PostgreSQL for persistence behavior; do not emulate its semantics.
- Add contract fixtures for every supported boundary version.
- Cover permission denial and redaction, not only successful authorization.
- Assert idempotency, rollback, conflicts, duplicate events, gaps, and reconnects.
- Keep golden files canonical, reviewable, and free of unstable values.
- Give every defect fix a focused regression test at the lowest useful layer.
